      "html": "<p>I make Quickler, so read this with that in mind. Every line about another tool comes from its own website, checked on 18 November 2026. Where I could not check something, I leave it out.</p><ul><li><strong>Fire Record</strong> (<a href=\"https://firerecord.co.uk/\" rel=\"noopener\">firerecord.co.uk</a>). Walk, talk and take photos on your phone; it drafts the full report, to PAS 79-1:2020 or BS 9792:2025, with an action tracker. Pay per report or choose a plan. <em>Better when:</em> you are a fire risk assessor who wants the report drafted from speech.</li><li><strong>AssessHub</strong> (<a href=\"https://assesshub.co.uk/\" rel=\"noopener\">assesshub.co.uk</a>). PAS 79-1, PAS 79-2 and BS 9792:2025 checklists, offline capture, floor plan pins, AI-assisted write-up, QC sign-off and branded PDFs. Priced per assessor, 14-day free trial. <em>Better when:</em> you run a team of assessors and want structured checklists with QC.</li><li><strong>Firehub</strong> (<a href=\"https://firehub.co.uk/\" rel=\"noopener\">firehub.co.uk</a>). Editable PAS 79 and BS 9792 templates kept up to date with industry input, offline work on a tablet, and a client portal for tracking actions. <em>Better when:</em> you want ready templates and clients who log in to follow up actions.</li><li><strong>Quickler</strong> (<a href=\"/pages/how-it-works.html\">how it works</a>). Your own fire risk assessment questions, answered in WhatsApp by voice note, text or photo as you walk. The report and action plan are written in your own Word or PDF layout. <em>Better when:</em> you already have your own report format, or fire is one of several assessments you write.</li></ul>"
    },
